Source/dependency classification
  Frozen tools/testing/selftests/net/ovpn/ovpn-cli.c:358-359 caps its read
  at 256 bytes before calling mbedtls_base64_decode at line 374.
  The original key is 349 bytes. The capped prefix has 253 base64 symbols
  (the other three bytes are newlines): 253 mod 4 == 1, an incomplete quantum.
  The complete file has 344 symbols and decodes to 256 bytes. A 255-byte
  diagnostic prefix contains 252 symbols and decodes the identical first
  189 bytes. That prefix is a control, NOT substituted test data.
  The small C case removes all kernel/network activity. GCC14, Clang19 and
  EvoCC at O0/O2 each pass all seven observations against the exact captured
  libmbedcrypto: 42/42. The one-symbol string "A" independently produces -44.
  This proves the newly exposed failure is in the frozen userspace helper's
  input truncation, not EvoCC kernel code generation. No library downgrade,
  changed key, patched original helper or accepted original PASS is inferred.
  Original closure would require a separately identified upstream/helper fix;
  the frozen-application verdict remains FAIL under the current contract.

